        "problem": "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in N:2{n}^{2}-30<2}?$",
        "worked_solution": "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $2{n}^{2}-30<2.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{n}^{2}-30 & <2 \\\\ 2{n}^{2} & <32 \\\\ {n}^{2} & <16 \\\\ \\sqrt{{n}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{16} \\\\ |n| & <4 \\\\ -4<n & <4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe natural numbers that are solutions to the inequality above are $1,2,3.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA={1,2,3}.\n$$",
